        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2251119?u=4f64df010a7037ceb8920034395f124132174636&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updates the \"example\" for <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FetchEvent#examples\" rel=\"nofollow\">FetchEvent</a> to improve clarity and better match likely real-world implementations.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When leveraging the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FetchEvent\" rel=\"nofollow\">FetchEvent</a> documentation to help educate my co-workers, the example provided lead to confusion about how to leverage the API. The improvements made should more clearly explain what is being done in the example and why each line matters.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">N/A</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">N/A</p>\n\n\n\n",
